er  emotional track  sober  [Music]  i went away i went on tour to europe  um i stayed clean kind of  like wasn't doing drugs but was drinking  a lot  etie spoke to the documentary's director  michael d  ratner and he opened up about why it was  so important to demi to lay it all out  on the table  i think she feels liberated i think she  feels like she doesn't have to walk  around  with a facade or wondering are people  going to pick up on this or  you know i've said i'm the poster child  for that but people evolve people grow  and you know there's no there's going to  be no aha gotcha moment after this she  says  i am a work in progress i've put systems  in place because i am a flawed person  here's where i am today and i'm i'm here  to tell you my journey when i came back  to la  after tour i picked up where  i had left off and i was  very heavily using demi overdosed and  was rushed to the hospital on july  24 2018. metro rescue 827  persons leaving does not want lasd  assistance and or help  i am not saying that i have not used  needles but that night i wasn't  injecting it i was smoking it  which is another reason why i was so  shocked when i woke up in the hospital  because i was like  no i'm not injecting it i can't overdose  on it  at the end of the day if you do too much  of anything it's gonna kill you her  objective was to  clear the air to tell her story to speak  her truth you could jump on live and  say whatever you're feeling that day but  that's impulsive and in the moment  whereas this  is you know you're gonna get to know  demi lovato through and through  in this piece

